# Git Flow Workflow

This project follows **strict Git Flow**. All changes must follow the branching strategy.

## Branch Structure

- **`main`**: Production-ready, stable branch. Only receives merges from `release/*` and `hotfix/*` branches.
- **`develop`**: Integration branch for ongoing development. All feature branches merge into `develop`.
- **`feature/<name>`**: New features or bug fixes. Branch from `develop`, merge into `develop`.
- **`release/<version>`**: Preparing releases. Branch from `develop`, merge into both `main` and `develop`.
- **`hotfix/<name>`**: Urgent production fixes. Branch from `main`, merge into both `main` and `develop`.
- **`chore/<name>`**: Maintenance and infrastructure work. Branch from `develop`, merge into `develop`.

## Branch Naming Rules

1. Use lowercase with hyphens: `feature/add-track-upload`, not `Feature/AddTrackUpload`
2. Include issue numbers when applicable: `feature/123-add-ogg-support`
3. Be descriptive: `feature/improve-genre-classification`, not `feature/fix`

## Important Rules

- **No direct commits** to `main` or `develop` - all changes must go through Pull Requests
- Feature branches **must** target `develop`
- Hotfix branches **must** target `main`
- Release branches merge into both `main` and `develop`

## Examples

```bash
# Feature branch
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/add-audio-fingerprint

# Hotfix branch
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b hotfix/critical-security-patch

# Release branch (maintainers only)
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b release/v0.2.1
```
